## 7. Emergency Rollback Runbook with Post-Rollback Reconciliation

> [!CAUTION]
> Execute this section only if the candidate deployment must be aborted.  
> **Important:** The original container `claimguard-staging-prephase1` uses in-memory H2 and **cannot** read the candidate's file-backed database. The procedure below guarantees that any claims created after deployment are preserved in JSON and on the intact volume.

```powershell
Write-Warning "================================================================================"
Write-Warning "[EMERGENCY ROLLBACK INITIATED] Restoring original container to port 8083..."
Write-Warning "================================================================================"

$rollbackDir = "E:\Desktop\Raj Yadav\Projects\backups\rollback-snapshot-$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd-HHmmss')"
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $rollbackDir -Force | Out-Null

# ==============================================================================
# STEP 1 (DATA PRESERVATION): Export Candidate Database State Before Stopping
# ==============================================================================
try {
    Write-Host "[ROLLBACK 1/5] Exporting post-cutover claims from candidate via API..."
    $candClaims = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8083/api/claims?size=100" -TimeoutSec 3 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if ($null -ne $candClaims.content) {
        $candClaims.content | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10 | Set-Content -Path "$rollbackDir\candidate-claims-export.json" -Encoding UTF8
        Write-Host "  Exported $($candClaims.content.Count) claims to $rollbackDir\candidate-claims-export.json."
    }
} catch {
    Write-Warning "Could not export via API (service may be non-responsive). Proceeding with volume preservation."
}

# ==============================================================================
# STEP 2 (STATE-CHANGING): Stop Candidate Container
# ==============================================================================
Write-Host "[ROLLBACK 2/5] Stopping candidate container..."
docker stop claimguard-staging

# ==============================================================================
# STEP 3 (STATE-CHANGING): Rename Candidate Container (Preserving for Forensics)
# ==============================================================================
Write-Host "[ROLLBACK 3/5] Preserving candidate as 'claimguard-staging-candidate-failed'..."
docker rename claimguard-staging claimguard-staging-candidate-failed

# Take physical offline copy of persistent database volume
docker run --rm -v claimguard-data:/data -v "$($rollbackDir):/backup" alpine cp /data/claimguard.mv.db /backup/claimguard-offline.mv.db 2>$null
Write-Host "  Database file preserved at $rollbackDir\claimguard-offline.mv.db."

# ==============================================================================
# STEP 4 (STATE-CHANGING): Restore Original Container Name and Start
# ==============================================================================
Write-Host "[ROLLBACK 4/5] Restoring original container to 'claimguard-staging'..."
docker rename claimguard-staging-prephase1 claimguard-staging

Write-Host "[ROLLBACK 5/5] Starting original container..."
docker start claimguard-staging

# ==============================================================================
# STEP 5: Verify Restored Service Health
# ==============================================================================
Start-Sleep -Seconds 5
try {
    $restoredHealth = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:8083/api/health" -TimeoutSec 5
    Write-Host "================================================================================"
    Write-Host "[ROLLBACK SUCCESSFUL] Original container is UP on port 8083."
    Write-Host "  Database: $($restoredHealth.database)"
    Write-Host "  Status:   $($restoredHealth.status)"
    Write-Host "================================================================================"
} catch {
    Write-Error "[CRITICAL] Restored container failed health check: $($_.Exception.Message)"
}
```

### Post-Rollback Data Reconciliation Guide
If new claims were created in the candidate before rollback occurred:
1. **JSON Snapshot:** Inspect `$rollbackDir\candidate-claims-export.json` for records with `id >= 6` (custom user claims created after baseline seeding).
2. **Database Offline Volume:** The file `$rollbackDir\claimguard-offline.mv.db` contains the full H2 relational state, documents, indicators, and audit records.
3. **Re-ingestion:** Once the root cause of the rollback is resolved in the codebase, the offline database file can be re-attached or the JSON records can be re-submitted via API.

